From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenBook <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: SystemUI: a shake needs real strokes, not touchpad
 jitter

GestureDetectionInteractor counted every change of sign in the
pointer's x movement as a reversal. A finger resting on a touchpad, or
the start of a tap, jitters by a pixel or two many times in 500 ms, so
ordinary touchpad use on the G14 kept invoking contextual search (Quire)
by accident.

A reversal now counts only once the pointer has come back at least
12 dp from its turning point. The 100 dp box, 500 ms window, three
reversals and cooldown are unchanged; the existing tests pass as they
are, and three new ones cover jitter, strokes below the threshold, and a
real shake that wobbles.

OpenBook ANAL-225 (Quire on the G14).

Change-Id: I844df39ad867472ca4ff833516608b8f08192446
---
 .../GestureDetectionInteractorTest.kt         | 46 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../interactor/GestureDetectionInteractor.kt  | 42 ++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 81 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/multivalentTests/src/com/android/systemui/contextualcursor/domain/interactor/GestureDetectionInteractorTest.kt b/packages/SystemUI/multivalentTests/src/com/android/systemui/contextualcursor/domain/interactor/GestureDetectionInteractorTest.kt
